To call `ippl::initialize` and `ippl::finalize` in a main program, you need to include `Ippl.h` and then invoke these functions with appropriate arguments. Specifically, `ippl::initialize` requires references to the command-line argument count (`argc`) and array (`argv[]`), along with an MPI communicator (`comm`). `ippl::finalize` does not require any parameters.

Example usage in a main program:
```cpp
#include "Ippl.h"
#include <mpi.h>

int main(int argc, char* argv[]) {
    MPI_Init(&argc, &argv);
    MPI_Comm comm = MPI_COMM_WORLD;

    ippl::initialize(argc, argv, comm);

    // Your simulation code here

    ippl::finalize();
    MPI_Finalize();

    return 0;
}
```

